=== Blocks ===
'''{{Animate|Brittle Ice (age 0) JE1.png;Brittle Ice (age 1) JE1.png;Brittle Ice (age 2) JE1.png;Brittle Ice (age 3) JE1.png|32px}} [[Brittle ice]]'''
* A fragile [[ice]] block that generates naturally in [[ice caves]] as part of [[crevasse]]s.
* Begins to crack when stood on by players or mobs, eventually breaking.
** [[Frostbite]]s and [[stray]]s can stand on brittle ice without breaking it.
* Does not melt, unlike regular [[ice]] and [[frosted ice]].
* Is created when [[water]] touches [[blue ice]].
** Any [[Water|water block]] that borders the [[Blue Ice|blue ice]] block horizontally will turn into brittle ice.
* Can be obtained when mined using a [[tool]] with [[Silk Touch]].

[[File:Calcite JE4 BE1.png|width=32x32]]''' Calcite block set'''
* Calcite now has several variants, which can be also crafted using a [[stonecutter]]:
** [[File:Calcite Pillar (UD) JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Calcite pillar]]
** [[File:Calcite Slab JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Calcite slab]]
** [[File:Calcite Stairs (N) JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Calcite stairs]]
** [[File:Calcite Wall (ewU) JE1.png|32px]] [[Calcite wall]]

'''[[File:Polished Calcite JE1.png|32px]] [[Polished calcite]]'''
* A block made from [[calcite]].
** Crafted using a 2x2 square of calcite.
* Has several variants, which can also be crafted using a [[stonecutter]]:
** [[File:Polished Calcite Slab JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Polished calcite slab]]
** [[File:Polished Calcite Stairs (N) JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Polished calcite stairs]]
** [[File:Polished Calcite Wall (ewU) JE1.png|32px]] [[Polished calcite wall]]

'''[[File:Polished Calcite Bricks JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Polished calcite bricks]]'''
* A brick block made from [[polished calcite]].
** Crafted using a 2x2 square of polished calcite.
* Has several variants, which can also be crafted using a [[stonecutter]].
** [[File:Polished Calcite Brick Slab JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Polished calcite brick slab]]
** [[File:Polished Calcite Brick Stairs (N) JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Polished calcite brick stairs]]
** [[File:Polished Calcite Brick Wall (ewU) JE1.png|32px]] [[Polished calcite brick wall]]

'''[[File:Chiseled Packed Ice.png|32px]] [[Chiseled packed ice]]'''
* A chiseled variant of [[packed ice]].
** Crafted using 2 [[packed ice brick slab]]s.
** Can also be crafted using packed ice or [[packed ice bricks]] in a [[stonecutter]].
* Depicts a snowflake pattern.

'''[[File:Chiseled Soulshale JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Chiseled soulshale]]'''
* Depicts the face of a [[singer]].
* Can only be found in [[ancient city]] loot chests.
* Can be obtained when mined without using a [[tool]].
* Currently unobtainable in the [[Creative inventory]], but is available via [[commands]].
* Is the first Sift-themed block to be added.

'''[[File:Ice Crystal.png|32px]] [[Ice crystal]]'''
* A crystal block which generates on the ground in [[ice caves]].
* Emits a [[light level]] of 4.
* Can be placed on all full sides of a block, and breaks if the support block is removed.
* Emits ambient sounds when placed above [[packed ice]].

'''{{Animate|Attached Icicle Base (D) JE1.png;Attached Icicle Middle (D) BE1.png;Attached Icicle Frustum (D) BE1.png;Attached Icicle Tip (D) BE1.png;Attached Icicle Tip Merge (D) BE1.png|32px}}{{Animate|Attached Icicle Base (U) JE2.png;Attached Icicle Middle (U) JE2.png;Attached Icicle Frustum (U) JE2.png;Attached Icicle Tip (U) JE2.png;Attached Icicle Tip Merge (U) JE2.png|32px}}<br>{{Animate|Icicle Base (D) JE2 BE1.png;Icicle Middle (D) JE2 BE1.png;Icicle Frustum (D) JE2 BE1.png;Icicle Tip (D) JE2 BE1.png;Icicle Tip Merge (D) JE2 BE1.png|32px}}{{Animate|Icicle Base (U) JE2 BE1.png;Icicle Middle (U) JE2 BE1.png;Icicle Frustum (U) JE2 BE1.png;Icicle Tip (U) JE2 BE1.png;Icicle Tip Merge (U) JE2 BE1.png|32px}} [[Icicle]]'''
* A speleothem block that generates as stalactites on the ceiling in [[ice caves]].
** Can also be placed on the ground as stalagmites.
* Can naturally grow up to 5 blocks long when pointing downward.
** Only grows under [[packed ice]] in areas with a low enough light level and outside [[the Nether]].
* Icicle segments melt (depending on the placement) at a [[light level]] of 5 or above or in the Nether, causing them to break.
* Function similarly to other speleothem blocks:
** Icicle stalactites fall when their supporting block is broken, and they deal [[damage]] to [[Entity|entities]] they collide with, which scales based on the distance they fall before impact.
** Landing onto an icicle stalagmite multiplies the fall damage taken, which scales based on the height fallen.
** Icicles can be broken by a thrown [[trident]].
* It can be placed in any direction and has a base, middle and tip variant.

'''[[File:Packed Ice Bricks JE1.png|32px]] [[Packed ice bricks]]'''
* A brick block made from [[packed ice]].
** Crafted using a 2x2 square of packed ice.
** Can also be crafted using packed ice in a [[stonecutter]].
* Unlike regular packed ice, it is not slippery.
* Packed ice bricks and chiseled packed ice belong to the Fast Sliding [[sulfur cube]] archetype.
* The correct tool to mine ice bricks is a [[pickaxe]], but unlike other ice blocks, it does not need [[Silk Touch]].
* Has several variants, which can be crafted using a [[stonecutter]]:
** [[File:Packed Ice Brick Stairs JE1.png|32px]] [[Packed ice brick stairs]]
** [[File:Packed Ice Brick Slab JE1.png|32px]] [[Packed ice brick slab]]
** [[File:Packed Ice Brick Wall JE1.png|32px]] [[Packed ice brick wall]]

'''[[File:Snow Bricks JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Snow bricks]]'''
* A brick block made from [[snow block]]s.
** Crafted using a 2×2 square of snow blocks.
** Cannot be crafted using a [[stonecutter]].
* Snow bricks belong to the Fast Sliding [[sulfur cube]] archetype.
* The correct tool to mine snow bricks is a [[shovel]].
** If mined with any other tool, or by hand, it will drop nothing.
* Has several variants, which cannot be crafted using a [[stonecutter]]:
* [[File:Snow Brick Slab JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Snow brick slab]]
* [[File:Snow Brick Stairs (N) JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Snow brick stairs]]
* [[File:Snow Brick Wall (ewU) JE1.png|32px]] [[Snow brick wall]]

=== Items ===
'''[[File:Arrow of Freezing JE1.png|32px]] [[Arrow of Freezing]]'''
* A [[tipped arrow]] which applies the [[Freezing]] effect.

'''[[File:Frostbite Spawn Egg JE1 BE1.png|32px]] [[Frostbite spawn egg]]'''
* Used to spawn a [[frostbite]].

'''{{InvSprite|Ice Ball}} [[Ice ball]]'''
* A throwable [[projectile]] that deals [[damage]] and [[Knockback (mechanic)|knockback]].
** Damage depends on how fast the projectile is moving which, like with other projectiles, can be influenced by how fast the thrower is moving.
* Breaks on impact with blocks or entities, creating a particle effect and sound.
* Can be used to brew [[Potion of Freezing|potions of Freezing]].
* Obtained from [[frostbite]]s, which have a chance to drop them when killed.

'''{{InvSprite|Music Disc Flurry}} [[Music Disc Flurry|"Flurry" music disc]]'''
* Added the "Flurry" music disc by [[Hyper Potions]].
** Has a 30% chance of being found in [[igloo]] basement chests.
** Has a [[comparator]] output of 7 when played in a [[jukebox]].

'''{{AnimateSprite|Potion of Freezing;Splash Potion of Freezing;Lingering Potion of Freezing}} [[Potion of Freezing]]'''
* [[Brewed]] using an [[awkward potion]] and an [[ice ball]].
* Applies the [[Freezing]] effect.

=== Mobs ===
'''[[File:Frostbite JE1 BE1.png|width=55x55]] [[File:Baby Frostbite JE1 BE1.png|17px]] [[Frostbite]]'''
* A [[zombie]] variant that can be found in [[snowy biomes]].
* Zombies [[Mob conversion|convert]] into frostbites when they stay in [[powder snow]] for 30 seconds.
** They will not convert if they are wearing a piece of [[leather armor]].
* Does not sink in [[powder snow]] or make [[brittle ice]] crack.
* Burns in [[sunlight]].
* It has two modes of attacking: a [[melee attack]] and a [[ranged attack]].
** Switches between melee and ranged combat based on target distance and whether they have [[ice ball]]s.
** Most frostbites use a standard melee attack, which gives the [[Freezing]] effect.
** Some frostbites spawn holding ice balls, which they throw as a ranged attack.
* Drops [[rotten flesh]] and [[Ice Ball|ice balls]] when killed, regardless if holding one or not.
* Converts into a [[zombie]] when underwater for 30 seconds.

=== World generation ===
'''[[File:Crevasse.png|40px]] [[Crevasse]]'''
* Small cracks in the terrain which generate in ice caves.
* Covered with [[brittle ice]] and filled with [[water]] below.

'''{{BiomeSprite|Ice Caves|scale=1.5}} [[Ice caves]]'''
* A cave biome that generates underneath cold biomes.
* It consists mainly of [[packed ice]] and [[calcite]].
* Large [[icicle]]s made of packed ice generate on the ground and hanging from the ceiling.
* [[Ice crystal]]s occasionally generate on the ground.
* Sometimes patches of [[snow]] can generate here.
* Does not generate [[glow lichen]], unlike other cave biomes.
* Ores generate inside blobs of [[stone]] and [[deepslate]].
* Common cave monsters along with [[stray]]s and [[frostbite]]s can spawn here.

=== Gameplay ===
'''[[Advancement]]'''
* Added one new advancement.
{{Load advancements|What Goes Around Comes Around}}

'''[[Effect]]s'''
* [[File:Freezing JE1 BE1.png|32px]] '''[[Freezing]]'''
** An effect version of [[powder snow]] freezing that causes an entity to [[freeze]], dealing [[damage]] over time and slowing their [[movement]].
** The Freezing effect will cause players to shake and eventually deal damage.
*** Causes those affected to slowly become frozen as if in powder snow for its duration.
** Wearing a piece of [[leather armor]] prevents the entity from freezing, just like with [[powder snow]], but will not keep the effect from being applied and will not remove the effect.
*** Being on fire or standing in [[fire]] or [[lava]] counters the Freezing Effect, similar to wearing leather armor.
** [[Undead]] mobs, [[Snow golem|snow golems]], [[Polar bear|polar bears]], and [[Ender dragon|ender dragons]] are completely immune to Freezing.
*** Mobs that are vulnerable to Freezing ([[Blaze|blazes]], [[Magma cube|magma cubes]], and [[Strider|striders]]) have a five times multiplier to the damage taken.
** Lingering potion, splash potion, and [[potion of Freezing]] can be brewed using ice balls.
** [[Arrows of Freezing]] can be crafted by placing a lingering potion of Freezing in the middle of the crafting table surrounded by eight arrows.

=== General ===
'''[[Block sound set definition|Block sound sets]]'''
* Added {{cd|minecraft:block_sound_set}} registry containing definitions for sounds produced by different categories of blocks.
** Format: object with fields:
*** {{cd|volume}} – a float between {{cd|0.00001}} and {{cd|10.0}}, the relative volume at which all sounds will be played.
**** If not present, defaults to {{cd|1.0}}
*** {{cd|pitch}} – a float between {{cd|0.00001}} and {{cd|2.0}}, the relative pitch at which all sounds will be played.
**** If not present, defaults to {{cd|1.0}}
*** {{cd|break_sound}} – Sound event, the sound that will be played when the block gets broken.
*** {{cd|step_sound}} – Sound event, the sound that will be played when an entity walks on top of the block.
*** {{cd|place_sound}} – Sound event, the sound that will be played when the block gets placed.
*** {{cd|hit_sound}} – Sound event, the sound that will be played while the block is being destroyed.
*** {{cd|fall_sound}} – Sound event, the sound that will be played when an entity falls onto the block.
*** All sound fields are optional.

'''[[Data component format]]'''
* Added {{cd|minecraft:dispense_behavior}}
** Determines what happens when the item is dispensed from a [[dispenser]].
** Format: Namespaced ID of a {{cd|dispense_behavior}} registry entry or an inline list of dispense behaviors.

'''[[Dispense behavior]]s'''
* A new registry folder: {{cd|dispense_behavior}}. Each file is a list of behaviors that describe a sequence of behaviors to attempt when dispensing an item. Unless otherwise noted, behaviors are tried in sequence until one succeeds.
* Each entry has a {{cd|type}} field specifying a dispense behavior type as described below, possibly with type-specific additional fields.
** Vanilla entries:
*** {{cd|minecraft:armor_stand}} - Used for [[armor stand]]s
*** {{cd|minecraft:boat}} - Used for all types of [[boat]]s, [[chest boat]]s, rafts and chest rafts.
*** {{cd|minecraft:bone_meal}} - Used for [[bone meal]].
*** {{cd|minecraft:brush}} - Used for [[brush]]es.
*** {{cd|minecraft:carved_pumpkin}} - Used for [[carved pumpkin]]s.
*** {{cd|minecraft:chest}} - Used for [[chest]]s
**** Only for regular chests, not trapped, copper or other types of chest
*** {{cd|minecraft:default}} - Used for any items without another specified behavior.
*** {{cd|minecraft:default_projectile}} - Used for all types of [[arrow]]s, all types of [[egg]]s, [[snowball]]s and [[ice ball]]s
*** {{cd|minecraft:dropper}} - No item has the default data component {{DCL|dispense_behavior}} with that id. Used for [[dropper]]s, regardless of the item, changing it modifies the dropper behavior for all items.
*** {{cd|minecraft:empty_bucket}} - Used for empty [[bucket]]s.
*** {{cd|minecraft:equipment}} - Used for all types of equippables except carved pumpkins and wither skeleton skulls.
*** {{cd|minecraft:filled_bucket}} - Used for all types of buckets with any contents.
*** {{cd|minecraft:fire_charge}} - Used for [[fire charge]]s.
*** {{cd|minecraft:firework_rocket}} - Used for all [[firework rocket]]s.
*** {{cd|minecraft:flint_and_steel}} - Used for [[flint and steel]].
*** {{cd|minecraft:glass_bottle}} - Used for empty [[glass bottle]]s.
*** {{cd|minecraft:glowstone}} - Used for [[glowstone]] blocks.
*** {{cd|minecraft:honeycomb}} - Used for [[honeycombs]].
*** {{cd|minecraft:minecart}} - Used for all types of [[minecart]]s.
*** {{cd|minecraft:potion}} - Used for [[potion]]s (note: only default potions, not splash or lingering).
*** {{cd|minecraft:shears}} - Used for [[shears]].
*** {{cd|minecraft:shulker_box}} - Used for all [[shulker box]]es.
*** {{cd|minecraft:spawn_egg}} - Used for all [[spawn egg]]s.
*** {{cd|minecraft:thrown_potion}} - Used for splash potions and lingering potions.
*** {{cd|minecraft:tnt}} - Used for [[TNT]] blocks.
*** {{cd|minecraft:wind_charge}} - Used for [[wind charge]]s.
*** {{cd|minecraft:wither_skeleton_skull}} - Used for [[wither skeleton skull]]s.

* '''Dispense behavior types'''
** {{cd|minecraft:brush_armadillo}}
*** Brushes an [[armadillo]] in front of the [[dispenser]].
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:charge_respawn_anchor}}
*** Charges a [[respawn anchor]] in front of the dispenser.
*** If the respawn anchor is already fully charged, no further behaviors are tried.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:convert_to_mud}}
*** Converts the block in front of the dispenser to [[mud]] in case it has the {{cd|#minecraft:convertible_to_mud}} block tag.
*** The item needs to contain a Water potion, otherwise it fails.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:drop_item}}
*** The item is dropped as an item entity.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:empty_bucket}}
*** Empties the [[bucket]] in front of the dispenser.
*** The item needs to be a bucket, otherwise it fails.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:equip}}
*** Equips the item onto a living entity in front of the dispenser.
*** The item must be equippable onto a slot of the entity.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:equip_chest}}
*** Equips a [[chest]] onto a tamed mob that can carry a chest in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:equip_sulfur_cube}}
*** Gives the item to a [[sulfur cube]] in front of the dispenser.
*** The item needs to be in the {{cd|#minecraft:sulfur_cube_swallowable}} item tag, otherwise it fails.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:fill_bottle}}
*** Fills the [[bottle]] from the block in front.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:fill_bucket}}
*** Picks up a fluid in front of the dispenser, filling the bucket.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:grow_plant}}
*** Grows a plant in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:ignite}}
*** Ignites the block in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:insert_into_container}}
*** Inserts the item into a container in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:place_armor_stand}}
*** Places an [[armor stand]] in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:place_block}}
*** Places the item as a block in front of the dispenser.
*** The item needs to be a block item, otherwise it fails.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:place_boat}}
*** Places a [[boat]] on water in front of the dispenser
*** The entity type is determined by the {{cd|minecraft:entity_data}} component of the item, and needs to be a boat, chest boat, raft or chest raft.
**** For any other entity type, the action fails.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:place_minecart}}
*** Places a [[minecart]] on rails in front of the dispenser.
*** The entity type is determined by the {{cd|minecraft:entity_data}} component of the item, and needs to be a minecart.
**** For any other entity type, the action fails
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:shear}}
*** Shears a mob or harvests a beehive in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:shoot_projectile}}
*** Shoots the item as a projectile.
*** The item needs to be a projectile item, such as an [[arrow]] or [[snowball]].
*** Additional fields:
**** {{cd|offset}} - vector of 3 doubles, the offset of the spawn position of the projectile from the center of the dispenser.
**** {{cd|scale}} - double, how far from the offset position to spawn the projectile, along the direction of the dispenser.
**** {{cd|uncertainty}} - non-negative float, the inaccuracy of the shot.
**** {{cd|power}} - non-negative float, the velocity of the shot.
**** {{cd|sound}} - optional object, the sound to play when shooting (defaults to {{cd|minecraft:block.dispenser.launch}} with volume {{cd|1.0}} and pitch {{cd|1.2}}).
***** {{cd|sound}} - Sound Event to play.
***** {{cd|volume}} - float provider, the volume of the sound.
***** {{cd|pitch}} - float provider, the pitch of the sound.
** {{cd|minecraft:spawn_golem_from_carved_pumpkin}}
*** Completes a [[golem]] in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:spawn_mob}}
*** Spawns the entity defined by the {{cd|minecraft:entity_data}} component in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:spawn_tnt}}
*** Spawns [[primed TNT]] in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.
** {{cd|minecraft:transform_block}}
*** Transforms the block in front of the dispenser using a block transformer.
*** Additional field:
**** {{cd|transformer}} - Namespaced ID of the block transformer to use.
** {{cd|minecraft:spawn_wither_from_wither_skeleton_skull}}
*** Completes a [[wither]] in front of the dispenser.
*** No additional fields.

'''[[Environment attribute]]s'''
* {{cd|minecraft:visual/has_sky_occluder}}
** Determines whether the sky occluder is enabled for the environment. The sky occluder will occlude the sky box up until a certain angle with fog color with a smooth occlusion border.
*** Value type: boolean
*** Default value: {{cd|true}} for the Overworld, {{cd|false}} for the Nether and the End.
*** Interpolated: no

'''[[Feature]]s'''
* Added {{cd|crevasse}} feature type
** Carves a winding, tapered crevasse into exposed terrain. The crevasse follows the terrain surface, extends in opposite directions from its placement position and requires a minimum connected footprint before carving.
** Format: object with fields:
*** {{cd|max_width}} – integer (between 2 and 8), maximum cross-section width in blocks.
*** {{cd|max_length}} – integer (between 4 and 16), maximum end-to-end length in blocks.
*** {{cd|min_footprint}} – integer (between 1 and 32), minimum connected horizontal footprint required before carving.
*** {{cd|cursor_surface_search_range}} – positive integer, maximum amount of blocks the cursor will scan downwards to find its next position.
*** {{cd|column_surface_search_range}} – positive integer, maximum amount of blocks each carving will scan downwards to find a carvable surface.
*** {{cd|twistiness}} – float (between 0.0 and 16.0), amount of horizontal curvature.
*** {{cd|tapering}} – float (between 0.0 and 1.0), amount of tapering applied on each step of growing the crevasse.
*** {{cd|turn_factor}} – float (between 0.0 and 1.0), intensity of rotation applied on each step of growing the crevasse.
*** {{cd|carve_depth}} – int provider, carve depth below the origin terrain surface.
*** {{cd|fill_depth}} – int provider, fill depth below the origin terrain surface.
*** {{cd|surface_block}} – Block state provider, block placed over the crevasse opening.
*** {{cd|fill_block}} – Block state provider, block placed at or below the selected fill depth.
*** {{cd|carvable_blocks}} – Block predicate, which blocks the crevasse is allowed to remove.
*** {{cd|acceptable_barrier}} – Block predicate, which pre-existing blocks to accept as part of a barrier.

'''[[Language]]s'''
* Added support for {{w|Javanese language|Javanese}} and {{w|Chavacano|Chavacano, Zamboanga}} languages.

'''[[Options]]'''
* Video Settings
** Added "Prefer DXGI Present", a new option that attempts to use DirectX to present the game.
*** The setting is only supported on the Windows platform, and not all hardware is supported.
*** The setting defaults to off, and it is classed as experimental; it may not work for all players.
*** With the setting enabled, the player may see improvements in IME support, improved support for Variable Refresh Rate, and experience faster alt-tabbing while the game is set to fullscreen mode.

'''Other Players'''
* A new menu which has been added to replace Social Interactions.
* Only available when playing on a world open to multiplayer.
** This includes:
*** Playing in singleplayer worlds open to LAN
*** Playing on dedicated servers
*** Playing on Realms
** Can be opened by pressing the "Other Players" icon button in the pause menu
** Can also be opened from in-game using the "Other Players" key ({{key|P}} by default)
* Lists the players currently online in the world you are in
* Lists players who are not online anymore, but may still be of interest:
** Players who were just online but left
** Players who recently sent messages in the chat
* Clicking on a player's icon in the list opens their Player Options.

'''[[Particles]]'''
* Added {{cd|minecraft:freezing}}.
** Emitted by entities which are affected by the [[freezing]] mob effect.
** Has no fields.

'''Player Options'''
* Player Options is a new screen accessible through both the Friends list and Other Players.
* It contains per-player social actions previously spread across the Friends list and Social Interactions.
* These actions are:
** Sending or canceling a friend request
** Accepting or declining a friend request
** Muting a player
** Reporting a player
* Muting a player hides their chat messages until the next time you start the game
* Blocking players is managed through Other Players.

'''[[Predicate]]s'''
* Added {{cd|below_heightmap}}
** Checks if the height of the position is below a given heightmap value.
** Format:
*** {{cd|heightmap}}: Heightmap type to compare origin against.

'''[[Shader]]s'''
* Added <samp>sky_occluder.vsh</samp> and <samp>sky_occluder.fsh</samp> shaders which are used to occlude the sky box up until the certain angle with fog color with a smooth occlusion border.

'''[[Sulfur cube archetype definition]]'''
