'''[[server.properties|Dedicated server properties]]'''
* Added {{cd|allowed-connection-ids}}
** A list of comma-separated ids.
** If non-empty, the server will match the values against {{cd|_id}} property in {{cd|minecraft:intent}} packet.
*** If there is no match, the server will reject the connection.
** This works both for both status and login connections, so any user connecting without the correct {{cd|_id}} in the server address will not see the status and will not be able to join the server.

* Added {{cd|enable-legacy-status}} field
** This option allows disabling existing legacy (pre-1.7) server status and ping protocol handling.
** To preserve existing functionality, value defaults to {{cd|true}}.
** Note: {{cd|enable-status}} needs to be set for any status information (modern or legacy) to be set.

* Added {{cd|key-rotation-period-seconds}} field.
** Determines the minimum duration after which server keys (used for establishing new connections) will be recreated.
** If set to {{cd|0}} a unique (i.e. ephemeral) key will be used for every connection.
** Default value: {{cd|60}}

* Added {{cd|status-contact-details}} field
** If non-empty, the value of this field will be sent in the {{cd|minecraft:status_response}} packet JSON payload under the contact property.
** This value is meant to be used to signal a way to contact the server owners about the server, even if there is no website or other information about it.
** This field is meant to be human-readable, but there are no other restrictions on field format.

'''[[Density function]]s'''
* Changed {{cd|upscale}} (renamed from {{cd|interpolated}})
** Samples the input function at a reduced resolution, and upscales on each axis with the specified modes. Modes that require more samples will generally perform worse. Upscaling is performed by axis in order: Z, X, then Y.
** Format: object with fields:
*** {{cd|input}} - Density Function, the input function to sample
*** {{cd|x}}, {{cd|y}}, {{cd|z}} - object with fields, the configuration for this axis
**** {{cd|mode}} - one of: {{cd|nearest_neighbor}}, {{cd|interpolate_linear}}, {{cd|interpolate_cosine}}, {{cd|interpolate_cubic}}, {{cd|b_spline_cubic}}, the mode to use.
***** {{cd|nearest_neighbor}}
****** 1 sample per axis.
****** Value is discontinuous across cell boundaries, gradient is always {{cd|0}}.
****** Values at cell vertices always equal the cell value.
***** {{cd|interpolate_linear}}
****** 2 samples per axis
****** Value is continuous, gradient is constant within a cell but discontinuous across cell boundaries.
****** Values at cell vertices always equal the cell value.
***** {{cd|interpolate_cosine}}
****** 2 samples per axis.
****** Value and gradient are continuous.
****** Gradient is {{cd|0}} at cell boundaries.
****** Values at cell vertices always equal the cell value.
***** {{cd|interpolate_cubic}}
****** 4 samples per axis.
****** Value and gradient are continuous.
****** Values at cell vertices always equal the cell value.
***** {{cd|b_spline_cubic}}
****** 4 samples per axis.
****** Value and gradient are continuous.
****** Values at cell vertices do not necessarily equal the cell value.
**** {{cd|cell_size}} - integer between 1 and 64, the size of each upscaling cell.
** Upscaling changed axis order from Z,X,Y to X,Z,Y.

* Changed {{cd|gradient}}
** The {{cd|from_coordinate}} and {{cd|to_coordinate}} fields now additionally accept a Vertical Anchor, as long as axis is {{cd|y}}.
* Added {{cd|domain_warp}}
** Samples an input function by applying an offset to each sampled coordinate.
*** Note: if the offsets change rapidly by large amount, performance may degrade significantly. This function should be used sparingly.
** Format: object with fields:
*** {{cd|input}} — density function, the input function to sample.
*** {{cd|offset_x}} — density function, the offset to apply to sampled X coordinates.
**** The result is implicitly truncated to an integer.
**** If not specified, defaults to: {{cd|0.0}}.
*** {{cd|offset_y}} — density function, the offset to apply to sampled Y coordinates.
**** The result is implicitly truncated to an integer.
**** If not specified, defaults to: {{cd|0.0}}.
*** {{cd|offset_z}} — density function, the offset to apply to sampled Z coordinates.
**** The result is implicitly truncated to an integer.
**** If not specified, defaults to: {{cd|0.0}}.
** At least one of {{cd|offset_x}}, {{cd|offset_y}}, or {{cd|offset_z}} must be specified.

