'''Network Protocol'''
* The server now more consistently disconnects clients when a packet they sent causes an error.
* The entity position synchronization packet now includes full-precision head rotation.

* Added {{cd|minecraft:mod_list}} custom packet payload
** This packet is intended to inform servers about client mods to simplify debugging.
** Vanilla client sends an empty packet at the start of configuration phase, as it does not know about any mods – that is still a responsibility of 3rd-party modding platforms.

* Modified {{cd|minecraft:intention}} packet
** The {{cd|host}} field in the serverbound intention packet can now hold additional parameters (previously it stored only the domain name used for connecting to a server).
*** The new format is similar to URI query strings – the domain can now optionally be followed by a {{cd|?}} character and then followed by {{cd|key{{=}}value}} pairs separated by a {{cd|&}} character.
*** Empty values can be omitted (including {{cd|{{=}}}} sign).
*** Keys and values are escaped according to the standard URI rules ("percent-encoded component").
*** Keys starting with {{cd|_}} are reserved for vanilla use.
*** Users can now input properties in any "Server Address" field in the server list.
**** Additionally, any address in form of {{cd|<id>@<host>}} will be parsed as {{cd|<host>?_id{{=}}<id>}}
*** If a server uses SRV DNS records, the host field will contain both original and resolved domains.
**** If the resolved domain is different from the original domain, the resolved one will be used as the "primary" one, while the original one will be added as {{cd|_o}} ("origin") property.
**** Example host string: {{cd|redirected domain>?_o{{=}}<original domain>:<original port>}}, while the port field in the intention packet will be set to the resolved port value.
*** The field size has been extended to 1024 characters.
*** Note: since the {{cd|minecraft:intent}} packet is unencrypted, properties should not be used for any security-sensitive purpose.

* Modified {{cd|minecraft:transfer}} packet
** Added {{cd|properties}} field – a string to string map of properties that will be added to the host field in the {{cd|minecraft:intent}} packet sent to the target server.

* Modified Login Protocol
** Encryption and compression must now be explicitly applied by the server by sending one of two packets that carry connection options.
*** The client must acknowledge the change with a matching packet.
*** Every packet sent and received by the client after the acknowledgement will use the new settings.
*** Previously changes were applied immediately on both sides, which might have lead to malformed packets.
** Packets that can carry options:
*** {{cd|minecraft:login_finished}} (clientbound) and {{cd|minecraft:login_acknowledged}} (serverbound).
*** {{cd|minecraft:apply_options}} (clientbound) and {{cd|minecraft:options_applied}} (serverbound).
** Changed encryption key establishment procedure.

'''[[Options]]'''
* "Graphics API" Video Setting:
** "Default": Vulkan is now the default graphics backend, rather than being randomized, and is no longer considered experimental.
** The game will no longer change the graphics API setting automatically if a startup crash is detected.

* Video Settings
** Separated the "Improved Fog" video setting from the "Improved Transparency".
*** Turning it on together with the "Improved Transparency" will behave the same way as the previous Snapshot with "Improved Transparency" enabled: both sky and clouds will be blended into the terrain render distance fog.
*** Turning it on without "Improved Transparency" will only blend the sky but not the clouds.
*** "Improved Transparency" can now used without "Improved Fog".
*** The performance impact of "Improved Fog" is minimal, but it may be noticeable on lower-end hardware.
*** The setting is enabled by default
*** It is disabled on the "Fast" graphics preset and enabled on the "Fancy" and "Fabulous" graphics presets.

'''Order-Independent Transparency shaders'''
* The OIT algorithm was simplified by replacing the wavelet-based mathematics with depth bin-based accumulation.
** Slightly improved performance at least on some devices.
** Reduced floating point precision issues on average.
** {{cd|OIT_WAVELET_RANK}} shader define was removed.
** {{cd|OIT_COEFF_COUNT}} shader define was replaced by {{cd|OIT_NUMBER_OF_DEPTH_BINS}}
** {{cd|OIT_COEFF_ATTACHMENT_COUNT}} shader define was renamed to {{cd|OIT_TRANSMITTANCE_TARGET_COUNT}}

