'''[[Shader]]s'''
* <samp>screenquad.vsh</samp> was renamed to <samp>screentriangle.vsh</samp> since it was actually representing a single triangle for a while now.
* Removed OIT (Order-Independent Transparency, controlled by "Improved Transparency" video setting) support from the <samp>clouds.fsh</samp>, since it is now used to render clouds when OIT is off and to render clouds to an offscreen target when OIT is on.
* Added <samp>blit_clouds.fsh</samp> shader with OIT support that renders clouds from an offscreen target to OIT targets.
* <samp>terrain.vsh</samp> is refactored to decode new vertex data packing.
** Terrain vertex data in <samp>terrain.vsh</samp> is now fetched from a texel buffer instead of traditional vertex buffers.
** The packing of vertex data for terrain chunk section mesh data has been changed.
* <samp>core/terrain.fsh</samp> was modified to support the separate "Improved Fog" video setting.

*'''Order-Independent Transparency'''
** OIT shaders were converted to rely on subpasses.
*** Changed <samp>core/oit_composite.fsh</samp>, <samp>core/oit_depth_bounds_cull.fsh</samp>, <samp>include/oit_depth_sample.glsl</samp>, <samp>include/oit_sample.glsl</samp>
*** Added <samp>core/blit_depth_bounds.fsh</samp> shader to blit depth bounds in a subpass context.

* '''Boat water mask shaders'''
** The way water mask is handled was changed to support subpasses in OIT.
*** It is now rendered to a separate target that is sampled during terrain rendering instead of being rendered to the terrain depth buffer.
*** Changed <samp>core/rendertype_water_mask.fsh</samp> and <samp>core/terrain.fsh</samp>
*** Removed <samp>core/blit_depth.fsh</samp>
*** This approach is used both when OIT is on and off.

