'''Validation'''
* Most validation issues in following registries no longer prevent elements from being loaded:
** {{cd|minecraft:loot_table}}
** {{cd|minecraft:predicate}}
** {{cd|minecraft:item_modifier}}
** {{cd|minecraft:slot_source}}
** {{cd|minecraft:context_float_provider}}
** {{cd|minecraft:context_int_provider}}
** {{cd|minecraft:villager_trade}}
** {{cd|trigger}} fields in {{cd|minecraft:advancement}}
** {{cd|requirements}} fields on {{cd|minecraft:enchantment_effect_component_type}} instances.
* The following issues are now considered errors that can prevent pack loading or cause command compilation failure:
** The validated element makes recursive calls to itself, either through tags or namespaced IDs.
** Any context values required by the validated element are missing from the context provided during execution.
*** For example, the modifier type {{cd|minecraft:apply_bonus}} (which uses the {{cd|tool}} context value) cannot be used in an {{cmd|item ... modify}} command which provides the {{cd|minecraft:command_modifier}} context (which lacks the {{cd|tool}} context value).
* Elements will only be validated if they do not have conditions or condition has all required context values.
** That means conditional elements can be used to avoid validation errors in loot elements used in multiple context.
** Conditional elements:
*** {{cd|condition}} field for cases in {{cd|minecraft:number_dispatcher}} (both {{cd|minecraft:context_float_provider}} and {{cd|minecraft:context_int_provider}} kinds).
*** {{cd|merchant_predicate}} condition field in {{cd|minecraft:villager_trade}}
*** {{cd|condition}} field in loot pools, loot pool entries and loot functions
* Validation errors will now prevent command compilation, both in functions and from the console
** For example, {{cmd|compute entity @s float {type: "minecraft:enchantment_level",amount:{type:"minecraft:linear",base:0.15,per_level_above_first:0.15&rcub;&rcub;}} will now fail to compile due to use of {{cd|minecraft:enchantment_level}} in a {{cd|minecraft:command_compute_entity}} context that does not provide required information ({{cd|minecraft:enchantment_level}}).
* The {{cd|minecraft:command}} context has been split into {{cd|minecraft:command_predicate}} (used for predicates in commands, like {{cmd|execute if predicate}}) and {{cd|minecraft:command_modifier}} (used for item modifiers, for example in {{cmd|item ... modify}} functions).
* To simplify the discovery of validation rules, a new report has been added {{cd|: loot_context_requirements.json}}
** Values given as {{cd|allowed}} for some context can be used by validated elements when run in this context.
** The context used by command arguments can be found in the <samp>commands.json</samp> report in the {{cd|context}} field of the following argument types:
*** {{cd|minecraft:context_float_provider}}
*** {{cd|minecraft:context_int_provider}}
*** {{cd|minecraft:loot_modifier}}
*** {{cd|minecraft:loot_predicate}}
*** {{cd|minecraft:loot_table}}
*** {{cd|minecraft:slot_source}}

